      "side": 1,
      "message": "This breaks if the shader has another declaration called `inner_result`. Instead of doing this and having the `if (i\u003d\u003d0) {} else {}` logic here, I\u0027d recommend assigning the whole `output.value` to a `let` declaration and then pulling the elements from that.\n\nSo you\u0027d generate code along the lines of:\n```\nlet tmp_clip_distances \u003d inner_result.clip_distances;\nwrapper_result.clipDistance[0u] \u003d tmp_clip_distances[0u];\nwrapper_result.clipDistance[1u] \u003d tmp_clip_distances[1u];\nwrapper_result.clipDistance[2u] \u003d tmp_clip_distances[2u];\nwrapper_result.clipDistance[3u] \u003d tmp_clip_distances[3u];\n```\n\nThere\u0027s an extra copy here, but I\u0027d imagine the MSL compiler would optimize it out, and we can do a better job of emitting this when we switch to the IR version of the MSL backend.",
